<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan weekly forex reserves down at $1.528 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan weekly forex reserves down at $1.528 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves were down at $1.528 billion on April 5, from $1.623 billion a week earlier, and against $2.413 billion on April 4, 1996, the State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Friday.</p>
<p>Following is the weekly foreign exchange reserves holdings position in Pakistan:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		APRIL 5    MARCH 29   APRIL 4, 1996</p>
<p>TOTAL			   1,528	1,623	2,413</p>
<p>Forex in Pakistan	     530	  561	1,347</p>
<p>Forex outside Pakistan	320	  384	  353</p>
<p>Gold coins and bullion	676	  676	  700</p>
<p>Special Drawing Rights	  2	    2	   13</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
